@article{cheng2020,
  author={Cheng, Ming and Cai, Kai and Li, Ming},
  title={RWF-2000: An Open Large Scale Video Database for Violence Detection},
  journal={arXiv preprint arXiv:1911.05913},
  year={2020},
  doi={10.48550/arXiv.1911.05913},
    abstract={
  	Problem Statement {
  		- The widely deployed cameras in public places e.g. Malls, Universities are mostly used to provide cues and evidence after crimes are conducted and are rarely used to prevent or stop criminal activities in time.
  		- Manually monitoring these cameras is time consuming and labour intensive
  		- It is expensive to monitor a large amount of video data in real-time manually to to wide adoption of cmaeras.
  		Elier methods relied on detecting anomly objects like gun shooting, blood, etc, rather than recognizing the activityit self.
  		- Exising models still have drawbacks of small scale, reduced diversity, and low image resolution.
  		- Some of the existing mnodels cannot genelrilze as they were traied on movie datasets which aren't close enough to real world abnomarl activities
  		- Most existing datasets are mainly composed of videos captured in a single scene, performed by actors, or extracted from edited movies.
  		- Existinf datasets suffers from one or more of these low image quality, lack of sufficient data amount, videos with long duration but crude annotations, and hybrid sources of videos that are not close enough to
realistic violence
- motion information may be useless due to the coarse pooling mechanism
  	}
  	Proposed Method {
  		- Proposed new dataset RWF-2000 with 2000 survellience videos from the real world, these videos were capured form youtuvbe to ensure diversity. Each video into a 5-second clip with 30 FPS
  		- Also proposed a model based on 3D CNN + optical flow (flow gated network).
  		- Th eproposed model is based on multi branch as it process both video frames and optical flow,
  		- The proposed solution adopt RGB images and optical flows to build the neural network, which can process the spatial and temporal information, lastly Flow-Gated
architecture can reduce temporal channels of input videos by self-learning, instead of traditional pooling strategies
  	}
  	Experimental Results {
  		- Used accuracy fro metric
  		- Proposed model achived 87.25\% accuracy
  		- The used dataset contained 2k videoes, of 5 seconds at 30 FPS, and train slit ration of 80:20.
  		- The used vide siuze was 64 × 224 × 224 × 5.
  		- The used opimizer was SGD optimizer with momentum (0.9) and the learning rate decay (1e-6).
  		- The propsed model had ~270k params
  		- Proposed modle was also tested on other datasets like Hockey, Movies, and Crowd and demostrated ability to generilizes
  	}
  	Strengths {
  		- The used dataset contains suvellience videos from the real world, ratehr than staged ones.
  	}
  	Weaknesses {
  		- Processing two similar outputs can be time consuming.
  		- The branhees of muti branch are based on similar 3D CNN
  	}
  }

}
